1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,446
Ever do more the day before vacation than

2
00:00:02,446 --> 00:00:03,098
all month?

3
00:00:03,148 --> 00:00:04,560
Congratulations.

4
00:00:04,610 --> 00:00:06,966
You're Specimen 002.

5
00:00:07,267 --> 00:00:09,111
There's actually a law for this.

6
00:00:09,161 --> 00:00:10,790
And by the end, you'll know how to

7
00:00:10,790 --> 00:00:12,290
use it against yourself.

8
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:13,608
Observe.

9
00:00:13,658 --> 00:00:16,135
Given a month, the specimen takes a month.

10
00:00:16,185 --> 00:00:17,494
Given one night?

11
00:00:17,544 --> 00:00:18,673
Forty minutes.

12
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,730
For three weeks, it reorganizes its desk.

13
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:22,659
Twice.

14
00:00:22,709 --> 00:00:25,093
Then, on the final night, it becomes a

15
00:00:25,093 --> 00:00:25,726
genius.

16
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,561
This is Parkinson's law.

17
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:30,569
Work expands to fill the time you give

18
00:00:30,569 --> 00:00:30,983
it.

19
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,664
A historian, Cyril Northcote Parkinson, wrote it in

20
00:00:34,664 --> 00:00:38,348
1955, as a joke, in The Economist.

21
00:00:38,667 --> 00:00:39,854
His punchline?

22
00:00:39,904 --> 00:00:42,598
As the British Empire shrank, the office running

23
00:00:42,598 --> 00:00:43,596
it kept growing.

24
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:45,601
Then scientists tested it.

25
00:00:45,651 --> 00:00:49,276
In 1967, people given extra time on a

26
00:00:49,276 --> 00:00:51,126
task really did take longer.

27
00:00:51,433 --> 00:00:53,920
With more time, we quietly aim lower.

28
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:54,676
Eh.

29
00:00:54,726 --> 00:00:55,905
Plenty of time.

30
00:00:56,233 --> 00:00:58,150
So use it against yourself.

31
00:00:58,200 --> 00:00:59,801
Give the task less time.

32
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:00,883
Set a timer.

33
00:01:00,933 --> 00:01:02,538
Bring the deadline closer.

34
00:01:03,733 --> 00:01:04,924
You're not lazy.

35
00:01:05,174 --> 00:01:07,380
Your deadline was just too far away.

36
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:08,636
This note?

37
00:01:08,636 --> 00:01:10,098
Written the night before.

38
00:01:10,098 --> 00:01:11,382
Perfectly human.
